          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How to change the object clause?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Hold Board Meeting, pass Special Resolution (75% majority) at EGM, file Form MGT-14 with ROC Haryana within 30 days. ROC issues fresh Certificate of Incorporation confirming the change. Process takes 15-20 working days. Patron handles the entire process for Gurugram companies."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What resolution is needed?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "A Special Resolution requiring 75% of shareholders present and voting at EGM. Higher threshold than the 50% Ordinary Resolution needed for capital changes. For closely-held Gurugram companies, achieving 75% is straightforward. For companies with multiple investors, pre-EGM consensus is important."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What is ultra vires and why does it matter?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Ultra vires means 'beyond powers'. If a company conducts business not listed in its MOA objects, those activities and contracts are potentially void. During due diligence, VCs check for ultra vires operations. Patron conducts proactive object clause audits."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How long does it take?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "15-20 working days from Board Meeting to fresh COI. For closely-held companies with 100% shareholder consent to shorter notice, 10-15 days. ROC Haryana processing: 7-14 working days after MGT-14 submission."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What documents are required?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Current MOA/AOA, Board Resolution, EGM notice with explanatory statement, certified Special Resolution, amended MOA with updated Clause III, Director DSC, and CS/CA certificate. Shorter notice consent if applicable."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can I add multiple objects at once?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. A single Special Resolution can authorise adding multiple new objects, deleting existing ones, and modifying others simultaneously. Patron recommends combining all planned amendments into one filing to save time and cost."
          }
        },
