                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-2">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What resolution is needed?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>A Special Resolution requiring 75% of shareholders present and voting at EGM. Higher threshold than the 50% Ordinary Resolution needed for capital changes. For closely-held Gurugram companies, achieving 75% is straightforward. For companies with multiple investors, pre-EGM consensus is important.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-3">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What is ultra vires and why does it matter?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Ultra vires means 'beyond powers'. If a company conducts business not listed in its MOA objects, those activities and contracts are potentially void. During due diligence, VCs check for ultra vires operations. Patron conducts proactive object clause audits.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-4">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">How long does it take?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>15-20 working days from Board Meeting to fresh COI. For closely-held companies with 100% shareholder consent to shorter notice, 10-15 days. ROC Haryana processing: 7-14 working days after MGT-14 submission.</p></div>
                    </div>
